s (Continued):** Urinary Tract Infection (UTI) and Pressure Sores / Injuries\n* **Physiotherapy Management After Surgery:** Assessment, Respiratory & Circulatory Exercises, Early Mobilization, ROM & Strengthenin\n<truncated 2391 bytes>\nnd their Indications\n* **X-Ray Interpretation Basics**\n* **Peripheral Arterial Occlusive Disease (PAOD):** Definition, Risk Factors, Clinical Features, Complications, Management, and Physiotherapy Role *(Note: Explored in more detail here than on Page 7)*\n* **Surgical Infections Classification:** According to Clinical Course, Site, Source, SSI Classification, and Presence of Pus\n\n### **Page 12**\n* **Anesthesia Types and Systemic Effects:** \n  * Types (General, Spinal, Local)\n  * Systemic Effects (Respiratory, Cardiovascular, Central Nervous, Gastrointestinal, Urinary, Musculoskeletal, Temperature)\n  * Physiotherapy Implications\n* **Cellulitis:** Definition, Causes, Features, Complications, Diagnosis, Treatment, and Physiotherapy\n* **Abscess:** Definition, Causes, Types, Features, Complications, Diagnosis, Treatment, and Physiotherapy\n* **Gangrene:** Definition and Causes\n\n### **Page 13**\n* **Gangrene (Continued):** Types, Features, Complications, Treatment, and Physiotherapy\n* **Tuberculosis (TB):** Definition, Types, Risk Factors, Features, Diagnosis, Treatment, Complications, and Physiotherapy\n* **Hospital Acquired Infections (HAI):** Definition, Common Types, Causative Organisms, Risk Factors, Modes of Transmission, Clinical Manifestations, Prevention, and Physiotherapy Implications\n* **Stereotactic Surgery:** Definition\n\n### **Page 14**\n* **Stereotactic Surgery (Continued):** Overview, Indications, and Complications\n* **Deep Brain Stimulation (DBS):** Definition, Overview, Indications, and Complications\n* **Rhizotomy:** Definition, Overview, Indications, Complications, and Physiotherapy Relevance\n* **Thalamotomy:** Definition, Overview, Indications, and Complications\n* **Neural Implants:** Definition, Exa